// Crack Hint — the "far too narrow" bark at the sanctum wall (DD-005)
//
// The Tiny Tar crack is a 32-unit gap in a stone wall. It is a fair puzzle
// only if the player can SEE that it is a way through and that they are too
// big for it; 32 units is about a third of a floor tile and easy to read as
// masonry damage rather than a door. Hrodny deliberately cannot help — she
// says the potions are "For the moment of miracles, they are, or so told, I
// was", i.e. she does not know what they do — so the connection has to be
// made at the wall, which is where the player is standing when it matters.
//
// This is a SEPARATE class from EggTempleEntry, and it has to be. In U8 an
// egg hatches at most once per fast-area load: Egg::hatch() early-returns on
// _hatched, and Egg::unhatch() is a Crusader-only no-op, so nothing clears it
// while the player stays put. One egg spanning both sides of the wall would
// therefore fire the hint at full size and then be spent — never setting
// templeOpen when the player came back through shrunken.
//
// Placed on the HALL side of the wall; EggTempleEntry (1456) sits on the
// sanctum side. Once the player is through, templeOpen silences this, and
// the class's only job from then on is to reopen the breach (below).
//
// FINDABILITY (2026-10-03). The bark names the gap as narrow but not
// where along 2,048 units of wall to look. build_map_18.py's rubble on the
// sanctum side (build_breach_rubble) shows over the wall from y 5620 on the
// hall approach and is the ground-level cue; the second bark
// points at it. (A grit plate on the hall floor was tried and removed: the
// wall hid it from the camera.)
//
// WHERE (2026-10-08, TODO "Lining up on the crack is fiddly", option C).
// Even found, the gap was hard to enter: the shrunken body (32 wide) has
// to stand with its x in 2848..2879, a 32-unit strip, and a walk step is
// 76-96 units. The strip starts at the east end of the shape-47 stub
// (box x 2753..2816), the 64-wide block build_map_18.py stands in the
// wall just west of the gap: it draws as a column of pale dressed stone
// against the rough glob wall, the only one on that line, and is in view
// from the hall approach with the rubble
// (docs/playtest-2026-10-01-breach-rubble/C1-*-zoom.png). So the hint
// names it: the crack lies hard against its east side. That sentence is
// spoken with the observation, and again on every hatch while the player
// carries Hrodny's potions, because that is when lining up matters.
//
// ONCE ONLY (2026-10-03). makeAvatarBig()'s teleport round trip resets
// every egg's _hatched in range, so with templeOpen still clear this egg
// re-hatched at the Tiny Tar regrow and barked again
// (docs/reviews/2026-09-30-four-anomalies.md finding 3). crackHintGiven
// records that the hint has been spoken.

uses "egg";
uses "flags";
uses "item";

globalflag templeOpen;
globalflag crackHintGiven;

eggclass EggCrackHint inherits Egg
{
	process hatch();
}

process EggCrackHint::hatch()
{
	item : Item;
	carrying : Number;
	firstTime : Number;

	// THE BREACH, RE-APPLIED (2026-09-26). Once the temple is open the
	// crack is a full-size doorway: EggTempleEntry destroys the six wall
	// records build_map_18 tags BREACH_QUALITY (307). Map 18's fixed items
	// are re-read from FIXED.DAT on every map switch, so the wall is whole
	// again each time the player comes back, and this class is what the
	// player crosses on the way in. Two eggs carry it: this one by the
	// wall, and a second at the hall's north doorway (y 4800) that reopens
	// the breach before it comes into view.
	//
	// getQ, not getQuality: walls are family 0, and I_getQuality answers
	// 0 for any non-SF_QUALITY family (COLPUZZL:180). Two loops, one per
	// shape; destroying inside a foreach is COLPUZZL's idiom too.
	if templeOpen
	{
		foreach item where type = TypeTempleWallPiece within 2000 of referent
		{
			if item.getQ() = 307
			{
				item.destroy();
			}
		}
		foreach item where type = TypeTempleWallStub within 2000 of referent
		{
			if item.getQ() = 307
			{
				item.destroy();
			}
		}
		return;
	}

	// The doorway egg is the breach re-opener only; the hint belongs to
	// the egg at the wall.
	if getY() < 5500
	{
		return;
	}

	// Once only: a re-hatch (the regrow) must not repeat the observation.
	// The guard covers these three barks alone, so a player who first came
	// here empty-handed still gets the potion nudge below on a later visit
	// with Hrodny's potions in the pack.
	firstTime = 0;
	if crackHintGiven = false
	{
		crackHintGiven = true;
		firstTime = 1;

		// Three short barks, one per sentence: each stays well inside the
		// 194x55 box (five lines), so no page can end on a dangling word.
		Avatar.bark("The stone here is split from top to bottom, and there
				is open air beyond it.");
		Avatar.bark("Grit has sifted down from the crack and lies heaped on
				the flags below it.");
		Avatar.bark("But the gap is no wider than my hand.");
	}

	// A stronger nudge only for a player who is actually carrying the
	// answer. Anyone who has not yet prised open Hrodny's chest just gets
	// the observation above, and no spoiler.

	// Once per hatch, however many she gave him: barking inside the loop
	// played the line once per potion, three times running with Hrodny's
	// three (docs/playtest-2026-10-03-batch-merge.md, finding 7).
	carrying = 0;
	foreach recursive item where (type = TypePotion) and (frame = 8)
	within container Avatar
	{
		carrying = 1;
	}

	// Where to stand (see WHERE above): with the observation, and on any
	// hatch while the potions are carried. It names the crack rather than
	// "it" because the potion-carrier hears it without the observation.
	if firstTime or carrying
	{
		Avatar.bark("The crack lies hard against the east side of the pale
				block set into the wall.");
	}

	if carrying
	{
		Avatar.bark("Hrodny's dark potions are in my pack. For the moment of
				miracles, she said they were. I wonder.");
	}
}
